<p>Philippine Vice President Sara Duterte said she will run for president in the 2028 election—an early move that starts shaping the next national contest in the archipelago nation. Her announcement comes as political pressure builds at home, including fresh impeachment efforts that have put her future in office under closer scrutiny.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Corruption allegations: Al Jazeera and Deutsche Welle report that multiple impeachment complaints have been filed against Duterte over corruption allegations.</li><li>Procedural twist: SCMP says Duterte was impeached last year, but the Philippines’ Supreme Court later threw out the case on procedural grounds.</li><li>Scale of the contest: SCMP puts the Philippines’ population at about 116 million people.</li></ul><blockquote>I offer my life, my strength and my future in the service of our nation. - Sara Duterte</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Sara Duterte: She said she will run for president in 2028, framing the decision as a pledge of service to the nation. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/politics/article/3343866/philippines-sara-duterte-throws-hat-ring-2028-presidential-run'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>BBC News (political context): The BBC places the announcement in the context of Duterte’s public feud with Marcos Jr after their 2022 election alliance. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn5g207k7d5o'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/18/philippine-vp-sara-duterte-announces-run-for-president-in-2028'>Philippine VP Sara Duterte announces run for president in 2028</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn5g207k7d5o'>Philippine VP Sara Duterte announces presidential run in 2028</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/politics/article/3343866/philippines-sara-duterte-throws-hat-ring-2028-presidential-run'>Philippines’ Sara Duterte throws hat in the ring for 